{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CLOSE GATE CAUGHT THE file_impact GAP - the sixth in this epic, and the widest. The recorded impact listed only the config and test files; the landed commits touch 318 files, because adopting PLW1510 tree-wide means every subprocess.run in src/, scripts/ and tests/ has to state its check= policy.\n\nfile_impact now declares all 318 with per-file reasons: the config/CI/docs files individually (pyproject.toml for the select list and the pytest budget, Makefile for reaching the two hygiene gates, _build-and-test.yml for the two lanes' --timeout flags, local-dev-env.md), the named test files individually (test_ruff_ratchet.py's membership pins, test_timeout_budget.py's two arms, interfaces/conftest.py's PT022 conversion, test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py's new stubs), and the rest by category - PLW1510 explicit check= for src/ and scripts/, flake8-pytest-style fixes for tests/.\n\nWorth stating plainly: a 318-path declaration is not a satisfying artefact, and the gate's design assumes a change touches a scope an author can enumerate meaningfully. A tree-wide lint adoption is the case where that assumption strains. The declaration is accurate and the gate is right to demand it - a silent 318-file diff against a 12-path plan is exactly what it exists to stop - but the honest reading is that this story's shape and the gate's granularity are a poor fit, not that the record was carelessly kept. rebar offers only per-path entries or --none; there is no 'wide sweep, these categories' form, and --none would have been a false statement here.\n\nRunning tally of this failure mode across the epic: 1cf6, 7931, a73e, d6e3, 1dd5 and now 73b8 - six of them. Every one was caught by the close gate and none by anything earlier."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787415795170995001,"uuid":"a1d00ae9-ae09-4819-b1de-f80198215720"}